WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.066 --> 00:00:00.633
Go to the ground.

00:00:00.633 --> 00:00:02.369
Fred Pleitgen has been on the front lines

00:00:02.369 --> 00:00:03.536
in Ukraine.

00:00:03.536 --> 00:00:03.937
And Fred,

00:00:03.937 --> 00:00:06.172
what are you seeing there tonight?

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:08.808
Are there and what we're seeing is that

00:00:08.808 --> 00:00:10.543
the fighting is drastically picking up.

00:00:10.543 --> 00:00:12.245
We saw some vicious battles

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:13.680
going on to the north of where

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:14.748
I am right now,

00:00:14.748 --> 00:00:16.683
massive exchanges of artillery

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.418
but also fierce ground

00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:20.487
fighting as well in force

00:00:20.487 --> 00:00:22.322
as the Ukrainians and the Russians

00:00:22.322 --> 00:00:23.356
are fighting for turf.

00:00:23.356 --> 00:00:24.591
Here's what we're learning

00:00:27.794 --> 00:00:28.962
Ukraine's entire

00:00:28.962 --> 00:00:30.997
eastern front is now heating up.

00:00:31.364 --> 00:00:32.332
This is Russian

00:00:32.332 --> 00:00:36.302
infantry in a massive firefight

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:36.970
in the forest

00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:39.606
near the town of criminal Donetsk

00:00:40.273 --> 00:00:40.974
close by.

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:42.976
We're creeping through the same forest

00:00:42.976 --> 00:00:44.544
with a Ukrainian frontline

00:00:44.544 --> 00:00:46.579
drone unit called Dnipro, one

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.381
that scouts out

00:00:48.381 --> 00:00:49.549
Russian positions and

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:51.117
direct Ukrainian fire

00:00:54.154 --> 00:00:55.088
Drone operator

00:00:55.088 --> 00:00:56.222
Ruslan says

00:00:56.222 --> 00:00:57.390
working in the forests

00:00:57.390 --> 00:01:00.960
is extremely dangerous.

00:01:01.027 --> 00:01:02.796
All time work intense.

00:01:02.796 --> 00:01:05.198
A lot of artillery from

00:01:05.198 --> 00:01:07.667
different directions, from

00:01:07.667 --> 00:01:09.803
east and from north.

00:01:09.803 --> 00:01:11.371
But the team is often able

00:01:11.371 --> 00:01:14.207
to spot attempted Russian advances here.

00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:15.175
Russian infantry

00:01:15.175 --> 00:01:17.877
are moving through the thick woodland

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:20.146
and this tank leaves cover and opens

00:01:20.146 --> 00:01:22.148
fire towards Ukrainian positions.

00:01:22.615 --> 00:01:23.716
That's mostly

00:01:23.716 --> 00:01:24.451
the Ukrainians

00:01:24.451 --> 00:01:25.351
liberated towns

00:01:25.351 --> 00:01:27.353
and villages in this area last autumn.

00:01:28.421 --> 00:01:30.457
But the scars of battle are visible

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:31.724
everywhere.

00:01:31.724 --> 00:01:32.325
This village

00:01:32.325 --> 00:01:33.860
like many of the ones in this area,

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:34.961
was heavily damaged

00:01:34.961 --> 00:01:36.529
when the Ukrainians moved in here

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:38.898
in fall. For a while, it was quiet.

00:01:38.898 --> 00:01:40.667
But now all that is changing.

00:01:40.667 --> 00:01:42.202
The fighting is coming back.

00:01:42.202 --> 00:01:44.771
And it's heavier than ever before.

00:01:44.771 --> 00:01:47.440
The few people remaining, those too poor

00:01:47.607 --> 00:01:49.876
or too old to flee are the new.

00:01:50.543 --> 00:01:51.411
I ask Valentino

00:01:51.411 --> 00:01:53.613
if it's not too dangerous to stay here.

00:01:53.613 --> 00:01:55.281
Yes, it is dangerous, he says.

00:01:55.281 --> 00:01:56.249
But what can we do?

00:01:56.249 --> 00:01:57.650
Of course it's dangerous.

00:01:57.650 --> 00:01:59.786
But we endure. Sometimes we hide.

00:02:00.053 --> 00:02:01.521
But now it's too cold at the base.

00:02:02.622 --> 00:02:03.256
The Russians

00:02:03.256 --> 00:02:04.591
have massively beefed up

00:02:04.591 --> 00:02:06.326
their forces around Crimea.

00:02:06.326 --> 00:02:06.993
They believe

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.862
they have to prevent the Ukrainians

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:10.063
breaking through here

00:02:10.063 --> 00:02:11.331
to sustain their own

00:02:11.331 --> 00:02:13.133
offensive against Bermuda

00:02:13.133 --> 00:02:14.567
and are now also launching

00:02:14.567 --> 00:02:16.369
fresh attacks near Vladimir

00:02:16.369 --> 00:02:17.370
further south.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.638
This video near Voulu

00:02:18.638 --> 00:02:19.772
shows Russian armor

00:02:19.772 --> 00:02:21.841
getting hit by Ukraine's artillery.

00:02:22.242 --> 00:02:23.943
The soldiers run away.

00:02:23.943 --> 00:02:25.411
A wounded comrade tries

00:02:25.411 --> 00:02:28.715
to crawl to safety in all these places.

00:02:28.715 --> 00:02:30.750
Drones are critical to detect

00:02:30.850 --> 00:02:33.686
and to destroy the enemy.

00:02:33.686 --> 00:02:36.089
Dnipro one has its own drone workshop

00:02:36.089 --> 00:02:36.990
where NATO's issued

00:02:36.990 --> 00:02:38.658
grenades are literally sawn

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:41.928
and have to be carried on drone launch.

00:02:42.262 --> 00:02:43.563
Yuri can manufacture

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:45.665
drone munitions in 20 minutes

00:02:45.665 --> 00:02:46.533
and they've proven

00:02:46.533 --> 00:02:48.401
very effective in the conflict.

00:02:48.401 --> 00:02:49.736
NARA's ordnance

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:50.570
drone operator

00:02:50.570 --> 00:02:51.704
is one of the most dangerous

00:02:51.704 --> 00:02:53.106
jobs, the boss says.

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:55.308
As soon as they locate a drone operator,

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:55.708
they use

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:57.977
all kinds of weaponry, artilleries

00:02:57.977 --> 00:02:59.512
and the last tanks.

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:01.381
We have a high rate of casualties

00:03:01.381 --> 00:03:03.483
among drone pilots, even a fixer here

00:03:04.884 --> 00:03:05.652
in the forest

00:03:05.652 --> 00:03:07.787
whose lands mission is now over.

00:03:09.489 --> 00:03:11.624
But he sees a long battle ahead

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:14.160
in a contest of wits and brute force.

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:16.563
Mostly

00:03:16.563 --> 00:03:18.932
last month, our arm exhausted

00:03:18.932 --> 00:03:20.433
but lost to think.

00:03:20.433 --> 00:03:21.534
Two weeks,

00:03:21.534 --> 00:03:22.769
maybe we stop

00:03:22.769 --> 00:03:25.138
and Russians making counterattack

00:03:26.306 --> 00:03:27.607
and all the time.

00:03:27.607 --> 00:03:29.709
Drones will shape the way

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:32.045
this war changes

00:03:33.947 --> 00:03:35.114
I think important to point out,

00:03:35.114 --> 00:03:35.648
Erin, that

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:37.350
what you heard there in that report,

00:03:37.350 --> 00:03:38.985
those thuds, those artillery thuds,

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:39.752
those explosions,

00:03:39.752 --> 00:03:40.353
we were on the ground

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:42.155
for several hours in that area.

00:03:42.155 --> 00:03:43.256
And it did not stop

00:03:43.256 --> 00:03:45.158
at any time that we were there

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:47.460
and we were witnessing all of that now.

00:03:47.594 --> 00:03:49.262
The Ukrainians say they believe

00:03:49.262 --> 00:03:50.530
what is actually going on there

00:03:50.530 --> 00:03:51.631
is that a lot of the people

00:03:51.631 --> 00:03:53.900
that Russia mobilized late last year

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:56.035
are now arriving at the front lines.

00:03:56.035 --> 00:03:57.136
The Russians are beefing up

00:03:57.136 --> 00:03:58.104
their presence there

00:03:58.104 --> 00:03:59.839
and they're going on the counterattack.

00:03:59.839 --> 00:04:02.141
And while this might not yet be the start

00:04:02.141 --> 00:04:03.476
of that spring offensive,

00:04:03.476 --> 00:04:04.711
they certainly believe it could

00:04:04.711 --> 00:04:06.079
be a prelude to it Erin.

